<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>dev.orwell</groupId>
        <artifactId>orwell</artifactId>
        <version>0.1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <groupId>dev.orwell</groupId>
    <artifactId>jarvis</artifactId>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>

    <!--
      Libraries first, then the four deployables. The split is by what each one costs to run, not
      by what it is about: the hub owns Postgres and the frame bytes, person detection burns CPU
      decoding images and talks to apps/alerting, the retention worker holds no port at all, and the
      frame viewer serves a browser. The first three used to be one process, which meant sizing one
      container for the most expensive.

      Only the hub takes frames over HTTP. Everything else that wants frames *watches* the hub
      through jarvis-frame-client, so a producer pushes each frame exactly once and the fan-out is
      the hub's job. That is why person-detection has no ingest endpoint of its own.

      frame-viewer is neither a producer nor a watcher: it reads frame_events after the fact, the
      way the retention worker does, because "what did this camera look like a minute ago" is a
      question about history rather than about frames arriving.

      fixture-detection is a second watcher, and it is separate from person-detection because they
      answer unrelated questions with unrelated configuration: one asks whether something appeared,
      the other tracks the state of named things that were always there. Adding a watcher costs the
      producers nothing, which is the point of the hub.
    -->
    <modules>
        <module>frame-core</module>
        <module>frame-client</module>
        <module>retention</module>
        <module>hub</module>
        <module>person-detection</module>
        <module>retention-worker</module>
        <module>frame-viewer</module>
        <module>fixture-detection</module>
    </modules>

</project>
